Q6  Hubble-frequency graviton quanta filling the Hubble sphere (hbar = 1)
PASS Q6a  N quanta of energy H in the Hubble sphere equal rho_L iff N = 1/(2 G H^2) = S_dS/(2 pi)  (Bekenstein S = 2 pi E R); N = R^2/l_P^2 gives 2 rho_L
PASS Q6b  the classical amplitude of that condensate is h0 = 2 sqrt(3) (Q1, f = 1, omega = H): a coherent state at h ~ O(1), outside linear/Isaacson control -- consistent with the literature's 'quantum-critical' condensate, and not a derivation of a0

